# API Design & Implementation

When creating or modifying APIs:

- Design RESTful, predictable endpoints.
- Validate all incoming requests.
- Return consistent response formats.
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes.
- Implement proper error handling.
- Avoid exposing internal implementation details.
- Separate controllers/routes from business logic.
- Keep business logic inside services.
- Keep database logic isolated.
- Ensure endpoints are idempotent where appropriate.
- Consider pagination, filtering, and rate limiting for large datasets.
- Maintain backward compatibility whenever possible.
- Document request and response formats.
